auth {
  mode: basic
}

auth:basic {
  username: {{SubscriptionId}}
  password: {{AuthorizationKey}}
}

docs {
  # HOMAG Connect API

  ## Rate limiting

  All endpoints are rate limited. If you send more requests than allowed within a time window, the request is rejected with `429 Too Many Requests` and is not processed.

  - The limits differ per application and endpoint and may be adjusted over time.
  - Wait before you retry. If the response contains a `Retry-After` header, wait at least for the indicated time; otherwise retry with an increasing pause (exponential backoff).
  - Reduce the number of requests by using paging, filters and caching.
  - The .NET clients can repeat rejected requests automatically (up to 3 times after 2, 4 and 8 seconds) if `RetryOnRateLimit = true` is set. This mode is optional.

  Details and a C# retry example: [Rate Limiting](https://github.com/HomagGroup/HOMAG-Connect#rate-limiting)
}
